# Keep the build context small and the image free of anything secret.
#
# node_modules is the big one: both apps' trees together are hundreds of
# megabytes, they are platform-specific, and the Dockerfile installs its own
# inside the image anyway. On this project they also live inside OneDrive,
# which makes reading them slow.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated inside the image. Copying a host build in would
# quietly ship whatever happened to be on disk.
**/dist
**/.output
**/.wrangler
# Bundled Worker: rebuilt in the image, and must never come from the host.
**/build

# Secrets and local state. .dev.vars holds the Google client secret; it must
# never enter an image layer. Pass secrets as environment variables instead.
**/.dev.vars
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Version control and editor noise.
.git
**/.git
.vscode
.idea

# Nothing here affects the build.
*.log
logs
docs
README.md
**/README.md
AGENTS.md
roadmap.md
scripts/pilot-*.mjs
scripts/pilot-results.json
scripts/test-*.mjs
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.https.yml
docker-compose.nginx.yml
Caddyfile
restart.sh
nginx/
.dockerignore
